# Force LF line endings on checkout regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout with the common
# `core.autocrlf=true` config converts every text file's LF to CRLF —
# harmless for most files, but silently corrupts values inside .env files
# (e.g. `apps/api/.env.example`, copied verbatim to `.env`): a connection
# string like `MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=...&schema=public` picks up a
# trailing `\r`, which breaks Prisma's URL parsing and surfaces as a
# confusing "authentication failed for `(not available)`" error that has
# nothing to do with the actual database credentials.
* text=auto eol=lf
